marimo 0.24.2  ·  public API only  ·  nothing is executed

PORTS — derived from the source, before anything runs
  load       inlets = —              outlets = df, pd
  normalise  inlets = df             outlets = norm
  gap_of     inlets = norm           outlets = gap
  histogram  inlets = norm           outlets = hist
  report     inlets = gap            outlets = —

WIRES — one per (name, producer, consumer). 20 lines of set intersection.
  df     load -> normalise
  gap    gap_of -> report
  norm   normalise -> gap_of
  norm   normalise -> histogram

ORDER — read off the same wires. No thread, no numbering, no stack needed.
  edit 'load'   -> re-runs ['gap_of', 'histogram', 'normalise', 'report']
  edit 'gap_of' -> re-runs ['report']
  'gap_of' and 'histogram' are siblings, so they run IN PARALLEL: True

STACK HONESTY — 'Stack this' is only offerable when the selection is a chain
  ['load', 'normalise', 'gap_of']                chain? True
  ['gap_of', 'histogram']                        chain? False
  ['normalise', 'gap_of', 'histogram']           chain? False

THE SINGLE-DEFINITION RULE — why the df outlet is well-defined
  added a second binding of df:  c7: df = df.dropna()
  get_multiply_defined()     -> ['df']
  get_defining_cells('df')   -> ['c2', 'c7']
  => the df OUTLET would have two producers. marimo refuses it, and so must a port.
